{% endif %}
```

## Approval Boundaries

- Ordinary reversible implementation work can proceed autonomously when it is already scoped and automated checks pass.
- Human approval is required for destructive or irreversible data operations, authentication or authorization boundaries, security-sensitive changes, secret handling, paid external services, production deployment, destructive schema migrations, major scope expansion, and infrastructure with significant operational or financial consequences.
{% if governance == "managed" %}
- Managed A2 work needs human approval before start. Managed A1 work can proceed, but cannot be completed without human approval.
- `make task-approve` is for humans only. AI agents must not autonomously record A1 or A2 approval.
{% endif %}

## Workflow

{% if workflow_mode == "local" %}
Workflow mode is `local`: agents may work in the current local repository.
Commits, pushes, and pull requests are optional unless requested.
{% elif workflow_mode == "branch" %}
Workflow mode is `branch`: agents should work on a dedicated branch. Commits
may be created, but pushing and pull requests are optional unless requested.
{% else %}
Workflow mode is `pr`: agents must work on a non-`main` branch, commit their own
changes, push to `origin`, and open a ready pull request. Do not push directly
to `main`.
{% endif %}

General reusable skills are in `.agents/skills/`. Codex adapter notes are in
`.codex/`. Capability skills, when selected by this profile, are under
`.agents/capabilities/skills/`.

{% if governance == "managed" %}
{% if workflow_mode != "local" %}
Before editing files, agents must be on a non-`main` branch. If the current
branch is `main`, create a dedicated branch for the task first.
{% endif %}

Managed lifecycle skills are in `.agents/managed/skills/`.
Project-specific context is in `project/` and `docs/`. Run
`make agent-pre-review TASK=<id>` before review, do not bypass controlled task
transitions, and keep dashboards synchronized and valid.
{% else %}
Project-specific context is in `project/brief.md`, `docs/`, and ADRs under
`docs/decisions/`. Keep changes small, run `make check`, and update the brief or
